00:15:43,270 --> 00:15:45,770
If she comes and sees me locked to this instead of the chair...

263
00:15:45,940 --> 00:15:49,480
...she's gonna know you were in here. So you might as well just let me go.

264
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:55,370
I'll clean your bathroom for a month.

265
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:55,370
Still wouldn't be clean.

266
00:15:56,410 --> 00:15:58,870
All I want is my freedom.

267
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:01,960
Foot rubs for a month.

268
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:01,960
Freedom.

269
00:16:02,120 --> 00:16:04,330
I'll take all your photos and put them into albums.

270
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:06,000
Freedom. I want my freedom.

271
00:16:06,170 --> 00:16:08,460
Why won't you hear me? Sophie, help me.

272
00:16:08,630 --> 00:16:10,880
Help me.

273
00:16:08,630 --> 00:16:10,880
Sophie, sit.

274
00:16:12,880 --> 00:16:14,840
God, would you just calm down?

275
00:16:22,100 --> 00:16:24,980
I'm going to say this for the last time.

276
00:16:25,150 --> 00:16:27,810
Would you please just...?

277
00:16:31,820 --> 00:16:34,400
Wow, there's a lot I didn't know about vomit.

278
00:16:38,240 --> 00:16:39,740
In a minute.

279
00:16:41,580 --> 00:16:42,910
So, what do you say, Joey?

280
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:46,870
You get the whole set of encyclopedias for $1200.

281
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:49,840
That works out to just 50 bucks a book.

282
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,880
Twelve hundred dollars?

283
00:16:53,670 --> 00:16:56,260
You think I have $1200?

284
00:16:56,430 --> 00:16:58,180
I'm home in the middle of the day...

285
00:16:58,350 --> 00:17:01,310
...and I got patio furniture in my living room.

286
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:05,890
I guess there's a few things you don't get from book learning.

287
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:08,190
Well, uh, what can you swing?

288
00:17:08,940 --> 00:17:13,030
How about zero down and zero a month for a long, long time?

289
00:17:14,030 --> 00:17:16,360
You don't have anything?

290
00:17:16,530 --> 00:17:19,160
You want to see what I got? Okay.

291
00:17:19,320 --> 00:17:22,580
I got a baby Tootsie Roll...

292
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:25,910
...a movie stub, keys, a Kleenex...

293
00:17:28,290 --> 00:17:29,880
...a rock...

294
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:32,050
...and an army man.

295
00:17:32,880 --> 00:17:36,300
Okay, I get the picture. Uh, thanks for your time.

296
00:17:37,180 --> 00:17:38,890
And a fifty.

297
00:17:39,050 --> 00:17:41,510
Huh. These must be Chandler's pants.

298
00:17:42,350 --> 00:17:44,220
For 50 bucks you can get one book.

299
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:47,350
What will it be? A? B? C?

300
00:17:47,520 --> 00:17:49,150
I think I'm gonna stick with the V.

301
00:17:49,310 --> 00:17:52,320
I want to see how this bad boy turns out. Heh.

302
00:17:55,990 --> 00:17:59,160
I, uh, will buy and wrap all of your Christmas gifts.

303
00:17:59,320 --> 00:18:01,070
No.

304
00:17:59,320 --> 00:18:01,070
Oh.

305
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:04,700
I, uh... Oh, I'll squeeze you fresh orange juice every morning.

306
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:06,410
With extra pulp?

307
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:06,410
Yeah.

308
00:18:06,580 --> 00:18:08,040
No.

309
00:18:11,750 --> 00:18:13,290
I've got it.

310
00:18:13,460 --> 00:18:15,630
You don't have it.

311
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:18,170
I have so got it.

312
00:18:18,340 --> 00:18:21,430
There's gonna be rumors about this. There's no way to stop it.

313
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:23,510
Sophie knows, Monica and Phoebe know.

314
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:25,720
How do Monica and Phoebe know?

315
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:25,720
Oh, I called them.

316
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:29,600
When they ask me what I saw...

317
00:18:29,770 --> 00:18:32,770
...I can be very generous...

318
00:18:34,440 --> 00:18:36,610
...or very stingy.

319
00:18:38,860 --> 00:18:42,870
Go on.

320
00:18:38,860 --> 00:18:42,870
I can make you a legend.

321
00:18:43,030 --> 00:18:46,990
I can make you this generation's Milton Berle.

322
00:18:47,870 --> 00:18:51,370
And Milton Berle has...

323
00:18:47,870 --> 00:18:51,370
Oh. Not compared to you.

324
00:18:55,710 --> 00:18:57,800
Well?

325
00:18:55,710 --> 00:18:57,800
They're not even touching the lasagna.

326
00:18:57,970 --> 00:19:00,010
Really?

327
00:18:57,970 --> 00:19:00,010
Oh, they love your casserole.

328
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:01,300
Yes.

329
00:19:01,760 --> 00:19:05,390
It's hard to believe, just a little while ago, this was nothing but ingredients.

330
00:19:07,560 --> 00:19:10,100
Everyone seems to like your dish.

331
00:19:10,270 --> 00:19:11,850
And you?

332
00:19:12,020 --> 00:19:13,940
I thought it was...

333
00:19:14,940 --> 00:19:16,440
...quite tasty.

334
00:19:17,690 --> 00:19:20,740
So if everyone liked it, and you liked it...

335
00:19:20,900 --> 00:19:24,200
...that would make this a success. Which would make you...

336
00:19:24,450 --> 00:19:25,910
A bitch?

337
00:19:27,410 --> 00:19:29,830
Well, I was going for "wrong," but we can use your word.

338
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:33,920
Yes, well, I was wrong.

339
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:36,250
And I have to say...

340
00:19:37,090 --> 00:19:39,050
...you really impressed me today.

341
00:19:40,840 --> 00:19:42,090
Wow.

342
00:19:42,260 --> 00:19:45,260
Um, you might even say that she pulled a Monica.

343
00:19:47,810 --> 00:19:50,270
She doesn't know we switched it.

344
00:19:51,350 --> 00:19:54,980
And the next time you cater for me...

345
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:58,400
...there will be nothing but ice in the freezer.

346
00:19:58,940 --> 00:20:00,940
Well, that really means a lot.

347
00:20:01,110 --> 00:20:03,200
Oh, Mom, don't bite your nails.

348
00:20:09,830 --> 00:20:12,040
Hello.

349
00:20:09,830 --> 00:20:12,040
Hey.

350
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:14,540
Hello, Chandler.

351
00:20:16,080 --> 00:20:17,710
I love you.

352
00:20:18,340 --> 00:20:19,960
Hey, what's going on?

353
00:20:20,130 --> 00:20:21,380
Oh.

354
00:20:24,380 --> 00:20:26,590
No, he doesn't.

355
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:30,720
Two hours, that lasted.

356
00:20:32,270 --> 00:20:34,230
So did you break up with Joanna?

357
00:20:34,390 --> 00:20:35,730
I think so.

358
00:20:35,900 --> 00:20:39,900
Well, it's a good thing you got out when you did, before she blew up like Vesuvius.

359
00:20:40,900 --> 00:20:42,400
The volcano?

360
00:20:40,900 --> 00:20:42,400
Yeah.

361
00:20:42,690 --> 00:20:47,700
And speaking of volcanoes, man, are they a violent, igneous-rock formation.

362
00:20:48,660 --> 00:20:49,740
What?

363
00:20:49,990 --> 00:20:52,700
Oh, yeah. Lava spewing, hot ash.

364
00:20:52,870 --> 00:20:54,710
Of course, some are dormant.

365
00:20:54,870 --> 00:20:57,920
Why are you talking about volcanoes all of a sudden?

366
00:20:58,090 --> 00:20:59,540
Oh, we can talk about something else.

367
00:20:59,710 --> 00:21:01,840
What do you want to talk about? Vivisection?

368
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:05,380
The vas deferens?

369
00:21:05,840 --> 00:21:07,760
The Vietnam War?

370
00:21:08,300 --> 00:21:11,310
Oh, did anybody see that documentary on the Korean War?

371
00:21:11,470 --> 00:21:13,430
Oh, yeah.

372
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:15,310
Oh, God, Korea's such a beautiful country.

373
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:18,690
With such a sad history.

374
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:18,690
Yeah.

375
00:21:19,150 --> 00:21:20,360
Could there be more Kims?

376
00:21:29,870 --> 00:21:32,240
Who's out there?

377
00:21:29,870 --> 00:21:32,240
It's me. Good morning.

378
00:21:32,410 --> 00:21:34,370
Rachel, could you come in here a moment?

379
00:21:34,540 --> 00:21:37,540
Yeah, sure. Um, they didn't have poppy-seed bagels...

380
00:21:37,710 --> 00:21:40,080
...so I have sesame ones... Oh, my word.

381
00:21:41,130 --> 00:21:42,380
I...

382
00:21:42,880 --> 00:21:45,090
I seem to have had a slight office mishap.

383
00:21:46,970 --> 00:21:48,840
Could you get the key off the back of the door?

384
00:21:49,010 --> 00:21:51,640
Yeah, sure. I...

385
00:21:56,180 --> 00:21:57,730
I'm so sorry.

386
00:21:57,890 --> 00:22:00,690
Tell your friend Chandler that we're definitely broken up this time.

387
00:22:00,860 --> 00:22:02,150
Okay.

